From: k30pro-linux-dualboot
Subject: [PATCH 0016] terminal: apply the keyboard inset unconditionally

The inset from patches 0013/0014 was gated on the text-input
input_panel_state event, but weston maps its virtual keyboard as a
permanently visible overlay panel and never sends that event - so the
prompt stayed behind the keyboard with only a few pixels of it showing.
Reserve the space always (measured: keys occupy the bottom 480 logical
pixels of the 540x1200 panel) and keep a CLI/ini opt-out via
keyboard-inset=0.

--- clients/terminal.c.orig
+++ clients/terminal.c
@@ -1093,12 +1093,17 @@
 	average_width = terminal->average_width;
 	side_margin = (allocation.width - terminal->width * average_width) / 2;
 	top_margin = (allocation.height - terminal->height * extents.height) / 2;
-	if (terminal->input_panel_shown && option_keyboard_inset > 0) {
-		/* lmi: align the bottom row with the top of the keyboard instead of
-		 * centring the content; rows that no longer fit scroll off the top. */
+	if (option_keyboard_inset > 0) {
+		/* lmi: keep the last row (the prompt) above the on-screen keyboard.
+		 * The inset is unconditional on purpose: weston maps its virtual
+		 * keyboard as a permanently visible overlay panel
+		 * (zwp_input_panel_v1.set_overlay_panel) and never sends the text-input
+		 * input_panel_state event, so there is nothing to gate on.  Measured on
+		 * the K30 Pro: the panel is 540x1200 logical, the keyboard + shortcut
+		 * bar occupy the bottom 480 px, hence keyboard-inset=480. */
 		int inset = option_keyboard_inset;
-		if (inset > allocation.height / 2)
-			inset = allocation.height / 2;
+		if (inset > allocation.height * 3 / 4)
+			inset = allocation.height * 3 / 4;
 		top_margin = allocation.height - inset -
 			     terminal->height * extents.height;
 	}
